      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Anima inpainting with Photoshop\n\nInpaints the selection of a Photoshop document with [Anima](https://huggingface.co/circlestone-labs/Anima) (a regular, non-inpaint model: the masked area is re-noised and sampled with the rest of the image as context).\n\n## Image Bench\n\n- **Load Image ib:img** receives the document image and **Load Image Mask ib:mask** the selection, both sent with the Image Bench Photoshop plugin (panel URL: `http://127.0.0.1:8188`). They are saved to `ComfyUI/input/` as `image_bench_photoshop_image.png` and `image_bench_photoshop_mask.png`, so send them once before the first queue.\n- `ib:cp`, `ib:pp`, `ib:np`, `ib:smp` work as in the other workflows: batch generation, model exploration and varying parameters inpaint the same image.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. In Photoshop, select the area to repaint (feather it a few pixels for a soft seam) and use **Send image and mask**.\n2. Describe the **whole image**, including the new content of the selection, in the positive prompt.\n3. Queue. **Grow Mask** extends the repainted area so it blends with the surroundings; **Image Composite Masked** pastes the result back into the original through the original selection, so everything outside it stays pixel-exact.\n\n## Tips\n\n- `denoise` 0.85-1.0 replaces the content, 0.4-0.7 keeps its colors and shapes.\n- Anima works best from 512 to 1536 px per side; keep the document within that range and its sides divisible by 16.\n- Turbo variant: 10 steps, cfg 1.0, sampler euler.\n\n## Model Links\n\n- text_encoders: [qwen_3_06b_base.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/circlestone-labs/Anima/resolve/main/split_files/text_encoders/qwen_3_06b_base.safetensors)\n- vae: [qwen_image_vae.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/circlestone-labs/Anima/resolve/main/split_files/vae/qwen_image_vae.safetensors)\n- diffusion_models: [anima-preview3-base.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/circlestone-labs/Anima/resolve/main/split_files/diffusion_models/anima-preview3-base.safetensors)\n"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
